# THE FOUR-TOWN CLUSTER RUN WITH ANOTHER TOWN'S GOAL IMAGE IN EXPLORE EPISODES (user 2026-11-15: "replace
# explore mode goal with random images from another town different from same environment").
# = slurm/cluster_frl_c0actor_privcritic_4towns_ar2_keepgoal_nojx_2m_par.env with ONLY:
#   FOREIGN_GOAL_EXPLORE=1 (vae_nav.debit_goal_wrapper, v34): an EXPLORE episode's goal image is a random
#   goal view rendered in a DIFFERENT training town of this same job (one pool per town, filled by the
#   training envs themselves, so no held-out scenery enters). Until another town has contributed a frame
#   (the first resets) the fallback is an own-town view at least WRONG_GOAL_MIN_M away, flagged in info.
# WHY: without it an explore episode showed the image of its own goal point 5-25 m ahead -- a reachable
# place that pays nothing -- and kept showing it for up to 1,000 decisions after the car had passed it.
# NOT set: HIDE_MODE_BIT (the actor still sees the mode bit) and v34's explore arrival bonus. The critic's
# goal inputs stay zero in explore. Goal episodes and every scoring overlay are unchanged.
# c0 was cloned with own-town goal images in explore, so the frozen phase (first 15,000 decisions) is also
# the check of what this input does to c0's own exploring: compare explore_m with the previous job's 208 m.
. "$REPO/slurm/cluster_frl_c0actor_privcritic_4towns_ar2_keepgoal_nojx_2m_par.env"
export FOREIGN_GOAL_EXPLORE=1
# +100 WHEN AN EXPLORE EPISODE HAS DRIVEN 200 M (user 2026-11-15: "add +100 when agent drives 200m").
# vae_nav.gated_reward's existing explore arrival: at EXPLORE_GOAL_DIST_M the step is paid
# EXPLORE_ARRIVAL_BONUS and the episode ENDS as "reached" (a fault on that step still wins). Was 0 m / 10.
# WHY: explore had no terminal reward, a fault cost -1 once and the lane cost ran every decision, so ending
# early was cheap: explore episodes fell from ~160 m to ~40 m locally and to 8 m on this cluster run.
# DISTANCE IS EXPLORE_DIST_MODE=net (the run's existing setting): 200 m STRAIGHT-LINE from the episode's
# start, not path length, because path length was farmed by circling one junction (v8, 2026-10-19).
# The critic's explore input has no distance-so-far, so it sees the bonus as a chance per decision.
export EXPLORE_GOAL_DIST_M=200 EXPLORE_ARRIVAL_BONUS=100
